app/Console/Commands/ScoutRecordCheckIns.php — in handle(), between the clarity_scout flag check and acquireConcurrencySlot():

if ($this->openAddressBookIsStale()) {
    return self::SUCCESS;
}

private function openAddressBookIsStale(): bool
{
    $freshnessMinutes = (int) config('scout.check_ins.book_freshness_minutes');

    if ($freshnessMinutes < 1) {
        return false;
    }

    $database = (string) config('database.connections.clarity_clickhouse.database');

    try {
        $rows = DB::connection('clarity_clickhouse')->select(
            "SELECT toString(max(refreshed_at)) AS refreshed_at FROM {$database}.scout_open_addresses"
        );
    } catch (\Throwable $e) {
        // A probe that cannot run is not evidence of a stale book, and the
        // per-kit matcher reads the same table one statement later, so a real
        // outage still surfaces there (same fail-open shape as
        // CloseInactiveShiftsCommand::latestGpsFor()). Warning/report here
        // would fire on every pgsql-bridge run.
        Log::info('scout:record-check-ins: book freshness probe unavailable — continuing', [
            'error' => $e->getMessage(),
        ]);

        return false;
    }

    $row = $rows[0] ?? null;
    $raw = $row === null ? null : ($row['refreshed_at'] ?? $row->refreshed_at ?? null);
    $refreshedAt = ($raw === null || $raw === '') ? null : Carbon::parse((string) $raw, 'UTC');

    // ClickHouse max() over an empty table returns the DateTime default
    // (epoch), not NULL — an empty book must read as stale, not as 1970
    // being merely old (CloseInactiveShiftsCommand idiom).
    if ($refreshedAt !== null && $refreshedAt->timestamp > 0
        && $refreshedAt->gte(now()->utc()->subMinutes($freshnessMinutes))) {
        return false;
    }

    $message = 'scout:record-check-ins: open-address book is stale — skipping cycle';

    Log::warning($message, [
        'refreshed_at' => $refreshedAt?->toDateTimeString(),
        'freshness_minutes' => $freshnessMinutes,
        'age_minutes' => $refreshedAt?->diffInMinutes(now()->utc()),
    ]);
    report(new \RuntimeException($message));
    $this->warn('Open-address book is stale — skipping cycle.');

    return true;
}

Use config('database.connections.clarity_clickhouse.database'), never a hardcoded 'clarity' — the local/worktree CH database is suffixed. Keep the ($row['k'] ?? $row->k) access shape the query classes already use. Update the class docblock: the matcher now reads the MV-backed book, the gate is the platform-side guard for a silently-aging full-refresh MV, and the schedule is live again.

